WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.220
What's up? Welcome to Models and Agents for Beginners, episode 57. It's June 1st, 2026.

00:00:06.740 --> 00:00:10.460
We've got some really cool AI stuff to talk about today. Let's dive in.

00:00:11.120 --> 00:00:15.360
So imagine texting a friend and having every single message from the start of the year

00:00:15.360 --> 00:00:20.560
still right there in the chat with no scrolling or forgetting. That is basically what just became

00:00:20.560 --> 00:00:26.960
possible thanks to a new model called M3 from the Chinese company MiniMax. This is the first

00:00:26.960 --> 00:00:32.900
open-weight system to reach top-level coding performance while also handling both images and text

00:00:32.900 --> 00:00:38.900
in the same chat. Open-weight means the actual numbers that make the model work get shared

00:00:38.900 --> 00:00:44.960
publicly. So anyone can download and run it themselves. Think of it like getting the full recipe for a cake

00:00:44.960 --> 00:00:51.260
instead of just buying slices at a bakery. You can tweak the ingredients yourself. The standout feature

00:00:51.260 --> 00:00:57.460
is its 1 million token context window which lets the model keep track of enormous amounts of

00:00:57.460 --> 00:01:03.420
information in one conversation. That changes things for students doing long research projects or

00:01:03.420 --> 00:01:09.220
writers building entire stories without the AI forgetting earlier details. It also challenges

00:01:09.220 --> 00:01:14.720
bigger companies because anyone can now access similar power without signing up for paid plans.

00:01:15.300 --> 00:01:20.400
For you personally, this could mean better free tools for homework help or creative projects

00:01:20.400 --> 00:01:26.580
once developers build apps on top of M3. Right now, the model is available for researchers and

00:01:26.580 --> 00:01:31.840
developers to download. So watch for simple web demos or apps that appear in the coming weeks.

00:01:32.720 --> 00:01:37.180
Okay, now for my favorite part of the show, the deep dive where we look under the hood.

00:01:38.380 --> 00:01:43.540
You know how when you are texting a friend, your phone only shows the last few messages before older

00:01:43.540 --> 00:01:49.440
ones scroll out of view. Now imagine the chat could hold an entire novel's worth of back and forth

00:01:49.440 --> 00:01:55.480
without forgetting anything from page 1. That is basically what a million token context window does.

00:01:55.840 --> 00:02:00.840
It gives the AI a huge short-term memory so it can reference details from way earlier in the

00:02:00.840 --> 00:02:07.300
conversation. The model reads everything as one long string of tokens where each token is roughly a

00:02:07.300 --> 00:02:12.700
word or part of a word and it keeps all of them active while answering. This works because the

00:02:12.700 --> 00:02:18.280
training process taught the model to pay attention to patterns across that entire length instead of just

00:02:18.280 --> 00:02:24.880
the newest lines. So when you ask it to continue a story, you started 50 pages ago. It can still

00:02:24.880 --> 00:02:30.500
remember the character names and plot points without you repeating them. Next time someone says context

00:02:30.500 --> 00:02:36.380
window, you can tell them it is basically giving the AI a bigger notepad so it does not lose track

00:02:36.380 --> 00:02:42.700
made a conversation. And that is basically how a million token context window works, not so scary

00:02:42.700 --> 00:02:47.840
right. Now let's move to some tools you can actually try yourself. First up is Scout,

00:02:48.420 --> 00:02:55.420
an AI companion that lives entirely on your old phone. A solo developer turned an unused Samsung Galaxy

00:02:55.420 --> 00:03:02.340
into a calm offline AI friend that listens, remembers conversations and stays family safe without

00:03:02.340 --> 00:03:07.540
any cloud connection. It runs completely on the device so nothing ever leaves your phone,

00:03:07.540 --> 00:03:11.420
which makes it feel more like a private buddy than a corporate tool.

00:03:12.620 --> 00:03:17.840
Teens or anyone who wants an always available companion without sharing data should keep an eye on

00:03:17.840 --> 00:03:24.100
this. It is heading to Google Play soon so search for Scout AI companion once it launches and try

00:03:24.100 --> 00:03:29.700
chatting with it about your day to see how the offline memory works. You may need a parent's help

00:03:29.700 --> 00:03:36.500
if age verification appears during setup. Next is Maven, a personal AI agent that feels like a

00:03:36.500 --> 00:03:42.540
helpful digital sidekick. Maven is an open project that lets you run a single AI brain across

00:03:42.540 --> 00:03:47.820
voice chats, messaging apps and scheduled tasks while keeping all your data on your own hardware.

00:03:48.560 --> 00:03:54.340
It handles long-term memory and background jobs without constant supervision so it can remind you of

00:03:54.340 --> 00:04:00.520
things days later or manage simple ongoing projects. Curious beginners who like the idea of a helpful

00:04:00.520 --> 00:04:06.320
digital sidekick should check the short demo video first. Go to the YouTube link in the original

00:04:06.320 --> 00:04:12.320
post and watch the voice interaction clip to hear how natural the conversation sound. Then visit

00:04:12.320 --> 00:04:17.760
the Maven site to read the simple setup guide if you want to try it later. Time for quick bits,

00:04:18.100 --> 00:04:23.920
the fast round of interesting updates. The fitness app Strava is now charging developers a monthly

00:04:23.920 --> 00:04:30.080
fee for data access after noticing too many AI tools scraping user routes and stats without permission.

00:04:30.560 --> 00:04:35.280
It is a reminder that the data we share on apps can be reused in ways we did not expect.

00:04:36.000 --> 00:04:41.340
Here's another quick one about how people use AI differently. One group treats AI like a

00:04:41.340 --> 00:04:46.700
vending machine. They grab the output and move on without learning why it worked. The other group spends

00:04:46.700 --> 00:04:52.460
an extra 10 minutes asking the AI to explain its choices which builds real skill over time.

00:04:53.240 --> 00:04:58.880
The second habit leads to higher pay and better work because judgment grows alongside the tool.

